/// \page fcg_extras_guide Extras library guide
///
/// Link the target \verbatim FCG-Framework::Extras \endverbatim
/// and include `<FCG/Extras/file_dialog.h>` for native desktop file and folder dialogs.
/// Extras publicly links Core and follows the framework's static/shared choice, versioning, and installation rules.
/// The \ref fcg_file_dialogs guide describes the completion interfaces and lifetime contract.


/// \defgroup fcg_file_dialogs File and folder dialogs
/// \ingroup fcg_components
/// \brief Owned C++23 future and callback interfaces over SDL's native dialogs.
///
/// \section dialogs_workflows Launch and completion
/// <tt>\ref fcg::showOpenFileDialog</tt>, <tt>\ref fcg::showSaveFileDialog</tt>, and
/// <tt>\ref fcg::showOpenFolderDialog</tt> accept owned <tt>\ref fcg::FileDialogOptions</tt>.
/// Launch on the main thread with SDL events initialized. The optional <tt>\ref fcg::Window</tt> parent is borrowed.
/// <tt>\ref fcg::Player::mainWindow</tt> provides the nullable main-window pointer for applets.
/// Locations and selected paths use native `std::filesystem::path`; conversion to and from SDL UTF-8 is explicit.
/// Filters own their labels and extensions. Extensions omit leading dots and may contain ASCII letters, digits,
/// hyphens, underscores, and interior dots. `"*"` is accepted only as the sole extension of an all-files filter.
/// Save dialogs ignore multiple selection. Folder dialogs ignore filters and permit multiple selection.
/// Platforms may ignore individual settings.
///
/// Futures become ready directly on SDL completion. Keep the future in the applet and poll it while processing events;
/// a continuous redraw request keeps the idle loop responsive while waiting. Balance that request when the result arrives.
/// \snippet file_dialog_examples.cpp future
///
/// Callbacks own their captures and default to <tt>\ref fcg::FileDialogCallbackThread::MainThread</tt> dispatch through
/// `SDL_RunOnMainThread`. Pump SDL events to receive deferred callbacks. Both native completion and main-thread delivery
/// can be inline. <tt>\ref fcg::FileDialogCallbackThread::SDLThread</tt> invokes directly on SDL's completion thread;
/// that can be a worker or the main thread. Callbacks must not throw.
/// See SDL's <a href="https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/SDL_ShowFileDialogWithProperties">dialog threading contract</a> and
/// <a href="https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/SDL_RunOnMainThread">main-thread dispatch contract</a>.
/// \snippet file_dialog_examples.cpp callback
///
/// \section dialogs_lifetime Pending native dialogs
/// Keep SDL and the parent alive until completion. Native dialogs cannot be cancelled through this wrapper, and destroying
/// a future neither blocks nor cancels. During shutdown, continue pumping events until the pending future is ready before
/// destroying its parent or shutting down SDL. Filter strings, native filter arrays, and completion data remain owned
/// through completion. Results do not borrow SDL strings. The wrapper starts no thread and owns no SDL initialization.
/// Android content-URI loading is outside this desktop filesystem API.
///
/// \section dialogs_errors Results and errors
/// <tt>\ref fcg::FileDialogResult</tt> is `std::expected`. Empty selected paths mean cancellation; the optional zero-based
/// filter index is present only when the platform reports an index within the submitted list. Failure returns an owned
/// <tt>\ref fcg::FileDialogError</tt>, categorized as invalid arguments, invalid launch state, or an SDL failure.
/// SDL error text is captured immediately. Empty callbacks throw `std::invalid_argument` at launch.
/// Callback exceptions, allocation failures inside SDL callbacks, and failure to dispatch a requested main-thread callback
/// terminate; exceptions never cross an SDL callback boundary. Allocation failures outside those callbacks may propagate.
/// The wrapper does not log.
